@startuml development
!include style.iuml
skinparam packageStyle folder
top to bottom direction
title LazyFinance — Development View\nSeven workspace packages; source dependencies, not network calls

together {
  package "apps/ui" as UI <<channels>> {
  }
  package "apps/api" as API <<application>> {
  }
  package "apps/persistence" as Persistence <<persistence>> {
  }
}
together {
  package "libs/rpc-api" as PublicRouter <<channels>> {
  }
  package "libs/rpc-auth" as Signing <<identity>> {
  }
  package "libs/rpc-persistence" as PrivateRouter <<persistence>> {
  }
}
package "libs/contracts" as Contracts <<finance>> {
}

UI ..> PublicRouter : types only
API ..> PrivateRouter : types only
UI ..> Contracts : public schemas
API ..> Contracts
Persistence ..> Contracts
API ..> Signing : sign
Persistence ..> Signing : verify
Signing ..> Contracts : context schemas
PublicRouter ..> Contracts : type references
PrivateRouter ..> Contracts : type references

UI -[hidden]right-> API
API -[hidden]right-> Persistence
PublicRouter -[hidden]right-> Signing
Signing -[hidden]right-> PrivateRouter

legend bottom
  |= Package group |= Responsibility |
  | apps/ui / api / persistence | Angular browser / NestJS workflows / private RPC and Kysely SQL |
  | rpc-api / rpc-persistence | Generated type-only router facades; no runtime server imports |
  | rpc-auth / contracts | Node-only Ed25519 assertions / public, internal and context Zod schemas |
  Services import public, internal and context schemas; the browser imports public schemas only.
  No application imports another application's source. Test-only router dependencies are omitted.
  scripts/rpc-generate.mjs reads API/persistence declarations and writes the two router libraries.
  Generation is explicit; build, type, architecture and drift checks validate source boundaries.
endlegend
@enduml
